        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify($json) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 120000,
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "responseFormat": "json",
              "neverError": true
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "a1b2c3d4-0004-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "POST /execute/telegram/callback",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [260, 0],
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "",
          "name": "TradeHub Engine token"
        }
      },
      "notes": "The engine re-loads the signal, re-checks the kill switch and re-runs the FULL Guardian Layer-1 gate before anything is submitted. The tap carries only an action and a signal id — it cannot bypass a check. Non-owner chats are rejected with 403. neverError is on so a 409 (already deployed) does not mark the execution failed; the engine has already answered the user in Telegram."
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
